SO IN JAVASCRIPT CODES LIKE 

OPTION 1:
alert('Hello');
alert('World');

OPTION 2:
alert('Hello')
alert('World')

THESE ABOVE BOTH THE OPTION CODES WILL EXECUTE SAME 
BUT CODERS DO PREFER HAVING SEMICOLON AT THE END OF COMMAND TO BE IN PRACTICE
AS THERE ARE SOME RARE SCENARIO WHERE JS FAILS TO INTERPRET NEWLINE AS SEMICOLON

EXAMPLE-

CASE 1:
alert("Hello");
[1, 2].forEach(alert);

OUTPUT FOR CASE 1-
    Hello
        1
        2


CASE 2:
alert("Hello")
[1, 2].forEach(alert);

OUTPUT FOR CASE 2-
    Hello
    TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '2')

HENCE TO AVOID SUCH SCENARIO PROGRAMMERS PREFER TO ADD SEMICOLON EVEN IF ERRORS ARE RARE 

*FOR QUICK COMMENTS JUST SELECT THE BLOCK OF CODE AND HOLD CTRL + FORWARD SLASH(/)*

*TO OPEN CONSOLE ON MAJOR BROWSERS LIKE CHROME, FIREFOX, EDGE, ETC F12 IS SHORTCUT KEY*

    